.TH FIREWALL-CONFIG-AUDIT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware M8.4.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
firewall-config-audit \- read-only Linux/BSD/Solaris/firewalld source inventory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B firewall-config-audit
.BI --source " SOURCE"
.RB [ --input " FILE|-" ]
.RB [ --null ]
.br
.B firewall-config-audit
.B --help | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads and validates one explicitly selected firewall source. No firewall
configuration or runtime state is modified. The command never escalates
privileges or interprets input as shell code. Native inspection supports
Linux for the Linux sources and OpenBSD/FreeBSD/NetBSD for their
supported BSD sources; Oracle Solaris SMF/PF/IPFilter sources on SunOS.
Offline fixtures work on any Perl test host.
.PP
Configuration and runtime observations are never equated. UFW INACTIVE
is not proof that kernel packet filtering is absent; nftables/iptables
snapshots can overlap when using iptables-nft.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --source " NAME"
Required explicit parser and native acquisition source. Supported values are
.BR ufw-config ,
.BR ufw-status ,
.BR nft-json ,
.B iptables-save
and
.BR ip6tables-save ,
.BR pf-info ,
.BR pf-rules ,
.BR ipfw-list
and
.BR npf-show ,
.BR solaris-pf-service ,
.BR solaris-pf-rules ,
.BR solaris-ipf-service ,
.BR solaris-ipf-rules4
and
.BR solaris-ipf-rules6 ,
.BR firewalld-state ,
.BR firewalld-active-zones ,
.BR firewalld-runtime-zones
and
.BR firewalld-permanent-zones .
.TP
.BI --input " FILE|-"
Read a stored firewall snapshot; a single dash means standard input.
Regular files are accepted only when not symlinks. If omitted, the chosen
native source is read using a fixed absolute path and read-only args.
.TP
.B --null
Emit eight NUL-terminated fields per row, with no header.
.TP
.B --help
Display help and exit successfully.
.TP
.B --version
Display version and exit successfully.
.SH OUTPUT
Tab-separated columns:
.B ENGINE SCOPE STATE FAMILY TABLE CHAIN POLICY RULES
(literal TAB separators). A dash means not available. Runtime nftables and
iptables inventories use state OBSERVED: a readable snapshot, not a claim
of successful firewall enforcement. UFW configuration uses ENABLED/DISABLED
and UFW management status uses ACTIVE/INACTIVE. PF info reports ACTIVE/
INACTIVE, PF main-filter and IPFW static listing counts are PARTIAL, and NPF
reports runtime ACTIVE/INACTIVE separately from configuration LOADED/EMPTY.
.PP
RULES counts source-specific rule objects, -A entries, or UFW display lines.
Do not combine counts or infer network reachability, firewall absence,
packet behavior, compliance, or host security from these rows. PF anchors,
IPFW dynamic state and the effective rules across multiple engines are NOT
reconstructed. Solaris SMF service states are NOT kernel activity,
IPFilter and Solaris PF counts are PARTIAL. Native BSD and Solaris output
compatibility needs real-host acceptance.
firewalld daemon RUNNING is not a verdict about kernel filtering.
Active zone bindings show neither individual source CIDRs nor interfaces.
firewalld runtime and permanent zone listings are separate PARTIAL views;
RULES is the count of explicitly displayed Rich Rules per zone only, not
services, ports, policies, direct rules, or all kernel rules. A zero count
and a zone target do not prove that any traffic is permitted or blocked.
.PP
See the English and German firewalld acceptance guides in docs/commands.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
One complete, validated snapshot, including empty sources.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line or missing/unsupported source.
.TP
.B 3
Missing backend, denied access, unsafe input file, command failure,
oversized, malformed or unsupported snapshot. No partial output.
.SH SAFETY AND LIMITATIONS
Only fixed read-only acquisition operations. Entire input is bounded to
8 MiB and validated before output. No individual filter rules, source or
destination addresses, comments or input paths are printed. Capture records
are not atomic across sources or kernel policy namespaces. Native BSD PF,
IPFW, NPF and Solaris SMF/PF/IPFilter sources are provisional.
HP-UX and IRIX are not yet implemented. Solaris 11.4 has PF, not IPFilter.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ufw (8),
.BR nft (8),
.BR iptables-save (8),
.BR ip6tables-save (8),
.BR network-service-report (1),
.BR pfctl (8),
.BR ipfw (8),
.BR npfctl (8),
.BR svcs (1),
.BR ipfstat (1M),
.BR firewall-cmd (1)
